          <div class="faq-answer-inner">Hail damage on asphalt shingles appears as round dark spots where granules have been knocked loose, exposing the black asphalt mat underneath. Common signs include dented metal flashing, vents, and gutters; cracked or shattered tiles; granule buildup in gutters and downspouts; and bruised shingles that feel soft when pressed. Hail damage isn't always visible from the ground, and many homeowners don't realize their roof is damaged until a leak appears months later. Happy Roof provides free post-storm hail inspections in Tampa Bay.</div>
